config MP2_PRODUCT_LIFETIME_S
	int "Seconds of uptime after which the image resets through PSCI (0: never)"
	default 120
	range 0 3599
	help
	  The image's own end: a PSCI SYSTEM_RESET at this uptime, so that a
	  counted standalone default (`default <image> N`) of it comes back
	  to Linux after N boots. 0 is a real product: no reset of its own,
	  it runs while the heartbeat holds. Only `forever` with
	  BOARD_PERSON_PRESENT=1 may carry such an image (README.md). It is
	  not the board layer's CONFIG_YAKOGL_STM32MP2_LIFETIME_S, which has
	  no off switch; a non-zero value must stay below that one (a build
	  assert).

config MP2_PRODUCT_PET_S
	int "Seconds between two PETs"
	default 5
	range 1 26
	help
	  Must stay under the timeout less OP-TEE's 5 s (a build assert).

config MP2_PRODUCT_HEARTBEAT_MS
	int "Period of the heartbeat timer (ms)"
	default 1000
	range 10 5000
	help
	  A k_timer advances the heartbeat counter at this period. The main
	  loop pets only when the counter moved since the previous PET, so
	  the period must be below MP2_PRODUCT_PET_S (a build assert).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
